1. Timestamps function:
It will helpful when we create a table and database
SHOW ALL - Which will show all the parameters of database
NOW() - It will show current time in non readablae format
SELECT NOW()
TIMEOFDAY() - It will show current time in readable format
SELECT TIMEOFDAY()
CURRENT_TIME - It will show current time
SELECT CURRENT_TIME
CURRENT_DATE - It will show current date
SELECT CURRENT_DATE
CURRENT_TIMESTAMP - It will show current data and time
EXTRACT - It will extract information from the timestamp
Syntax:SELECT EXTRACT(DAY FROM col_name) FROM table_name;
EG: SELECT EXTRACT(QUARTER FROM payment_date) FROM payment;
AGE - It will show the age of the timestamp
Syntax: SELECT AGE(col_name) FROM table_name;
EG: SELECT AGE(payment_date) FROM payment;
TO_CHAR - It will convert anything like integer or timestamp into string - DOC - https://www.postgresql.org/docs/12/functions-formatting.html
Syntax:  SELECT TO_CHAR(col_name, 'format ie YYYY_MM_DD') FROM table_name;
EG:SELECT TO_CHAR(payment_date, 'YYYY-MM-DD') FROM payment;

2. Mathemetical Function - We can directly use in select statement like below
