Its stright forward using in select statement for perform all our operations and we can use alias as well

3. String function - We can manipulate the data, we can use in select statement like below
SELECT length(LOWER(LEFT(first_name,1)) || '_' || LOWER(last_name)||'@dell.com') AS emp_email from customer; - Here || for concatinate, Length, lowercase etc

4. SubQuery - We can pass the output of one query to input of another query. If the output of subquery returns one row we can use comparision operator in where clause, if its return multiple rows then need to use IN clause.Always subquery execute first and subquery should be given in ()
Syntax: select col_name from table name where col_name > (select avg(col_name) from table_name); here its an example for comparision operator because avg return one row
Eg:
SELECT film_id,title, rental_rate FROM film WHERE rental_rate > (SELECT ROUND(AVG(rental_rate),2) FROM film) ORDER BY film_id;
Syntax: select col_name from table name where col_name IN (select col_name from table_name); here its an example for IN operator because it return multiple row
EG:
SELECT title FROM film WHERE film_id IN (SELECT inventory.film_id FROM rental INNER JOIN inventory ON rental.inventory_id = inventory.inventory_id WHERE return_date BETWEEN '2005-05-28' AND '2005-05-30');
EXISTS() - Its used to check if subquery returned any row or not
Syntax:
select col_name from table name where EXISTS(select avg(col_name) from table_name);
Eg:
SELECT first_name, last_name
FROM customer c
WHERE EXISTS (
    SELECT * FROM payment p
    WHERE p.customer_id = c.customer_id AND p.amount > 11
);


 - This query returns the first name and last name of customers who have made at least one payment with an amount greater than 11.
 A correlated subquery is a subquery that references a column from the outer (main) query. Because of this reference, the subquery is executed once for each row of the outer query. Above we used corellected sub query
 A correlated subquery is a subquery that refers to a column from the outer query. In this case:
c.customer_id is from the outer query (customer table).
It's being used inside the subquery on the paymx`ent table.
This means:
For each row in the customer table, the subquery is run to check if there is any matching payment where the amount is greater than 11.

5. Self Join: Its usually join within the table. When we want to compare the values of column of rows with in the table then self join used.Matches rows within same table

Syntax:
SELECT tablea.col_name, tableb.col_name FROM table_name AS tablea JOIN table_name AS tableb ON tablea.col_name = tableb.col_name
SELECT f1.title, f2.title, f1.length
FROM film AS f1
JOIN film AS f2
  ON f1.film_id != f2.film_id
  AND f1.length = f2.length;
